---
layout: article
title: Quick start
description: Choose an Appwrite partner integration model and take your first steps with OAuth connect or organization API keys.
---

This quick start helps you pick the right integration path and wire up your first Console API call.

# Choose your integration model {% #choose-your-integration-model %}

| Model | Best for | Auth |
| ----- | -------- | ---- |
| [OAuth connect](/docs/partners/oauth-connect) | Users link existing Appwrite accounts | User consent via OAuth 2.0 |
| [Org API keys](/docs/partners/org-api-keys) | Your platform provisions resources in your org | Organization API key |

Use **OAuth connect** when your customers already use Appwrite and want to grant your product access to their organizations.

Use **org API keys** when your platform creates and manages Appwrite projects, domains, and resources inside an organization you control.

# Prerequisites {% #prerequisites %}

- An Appwrite Cloud account with an organization
- A server-side environment to store secrets (API keys or OAuth client credentials)
- The [Appwrite Console SDK](/docs/sdks) for Node.js, Python, or another server language

# Step 1: Initialize the Console SDK {% #step-1-initialize-the-console-sdk %}

Partner integrations run on your backend. Initialize the Console SDK with your session or an organization API key:

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
import { Client, Organizations, Projects } from 'node-appwrite';

const client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('console');

// With an organization API key (server-to-server)
client.setKey(process.env.APPWRITE_ORG_API_KEY);

const organizations = new Organizations(client);
const projects = new Projects(client);
```
```server-python
from appwrite.client import Client
from appwrite.services.organizations import Organizations
from appwrite.services.projects import Projects

client = Client()
client.set_endpoint('https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
client.set_project('console')
client.set_key(os.environ['APPWRITE_ORG_API_KEY'])

organizations = Organizations(client)
projects = Projects(client)
```
{% /multicode %}

{% info title="Never expose secrets in client apps" %}
Organization API keys and OAuth client secrets must stay on your server. Use your backend to call Console APIs and project APIs on behalf of users.
{% /info %}

# Step 2: List or create a project {% #step-2-list-or-create-a-project %}

With an org API key, list projects in your organization or create one for a new customer:

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const list = await projects.list({
    queries: [],
});

const created = await projects.create({
    projectId: 'unique()',
    name: 'Customer workspace',
    teamId: '<ORGANIZATION_ID>',
    region: 'fra',
});
```
{% /multicode %}

# Step 3: Manage project resources {% #step-3-manage-project-resources %}

After you have a project, use the project SDK with a project API key or dynamic key to manage databases, storage, functions, and other services inside that project. See [Manage resources](/docs/partners/projects/resources).

